+## HTTPS
+
+To serve the REST API, UI, and gRPC over TLS, set the protocol and provide a certificate and matching private key. Flipt checks that both paths exist during configuration and loads the key pair before starting listeners.
+
+```yaml
+server:
+  protocol: https
+  https_port: 443
+  grpc_port: 9000
+  cert_file: /etc/flipt/tls/server.crt
+  cert_key: /etc/flipt/tls/server.key
+```
+
+The REST API and UI use `https_port`; gRPC continues to use `grpc_port`. The `http_port` setting is used only when `protocol` is `http`.
+
 ## Databases
 
 Flipt supports both [SQLite](https://www.sqlite.org/index.html) and [Postgres](https://www.postgresql.org/) databases as of `v0.5.0`.
